	<key>NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription</key>
	<string>To change the volume of a single app, macOS passes that app's sound through MaxCandela, which plays it back at the level you choose. The sound is processed live on this Mac — it is never recorded, saved or sent anywhere — and only apps you adjust are affected.</string>
	<key>NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
	<string>MaxCandela lists the Bluetooth devices paired with this Mac so you can connect and disconnect them from the menu bar, and shows the battery level of devices that report one. Nothing about your devices is stored or sent anywhere.</string>
	<key>NSCalendarsFullAccessUsageDescription</key>
	<string>MaxCandela shows your upcoming meetings in its menu and lets you join calls with one click. Your calendar is read on this Mac only and is never sent anywhere.</string>
